  "narrative": "The new results substantially refine the residual feature_063 signal while confirming that many other residual screens are null. All feature_063 claims are direction -1, so positive signed estimates mean feature_063=1 is associated with lower outcome_001 than feature_063=0; for threshold-level support I required both the signed point estimate and signed lower 95% interval bound to exceed 0.15 units.\n\nH165 gives the strongest new feature_063 evidence: signed estimate +0.315, signed interval +0.218 to +0.412, with n=98 exposed and 658 comparator. This is a complementary focal-negative context to the near-null feature_041-positive check H157, and the lower bound is comfortably above threshold. I accept H165 and keep it active because independent validation is warranted for a residual, multiplicity-heavy comparison. H166 also reaches threshold: +0.303, lower +0.190, in focal-negative low feature_030. H168 also reaches threshold: +0.280, lower +0.186, in focal-negative high feature_040 after excluding feature_003. These two add context support, but they share overlapping focal-negative population and correlated residual-marker structure, so they should not be counted as fully independent replications of feature_063. I accept both in the supplied dataset while retaining caution about generalization and co-marker confounding.\n\nH167 and H169 are positive but not threshold-level. H167 has signed estimate +0.207 with lower +0.109, and H169 has +0.164 with lower +0.101. Their intervals do not reach the claimed effect-size threshold, though they are entirely positive and therefore remain suggestive context checks rather than firm accepted findings. I leave them unresolved and active because they inform the boundary of the feature_063 signal without supporting threshold-level conclusions.\n\nThe continuous and common binary residual screens are not compelling. H20, feature_019 55 versus 45 in the negative direction, has a signed estimate +0.240 but interval -0.036 to +0.517 and very small cells; it does not support a meaningful direction-specific difference and is rejected. H28, H29, H37, and H45 are near null with intervals spanning the claimed direction and below threshold, so they are rejected and closed. H104 and H126 remain infeasible diagnostic-only failures due insufficient cell counts, so they are unresolved and deferred rather than evidence of nullity.\n\nMultiplicity and confounding remain central criticisms. The residual feature_063 cluster emerged after many context screens, and overlapping comparisons cannot be treated as independent. H168 specifically tests whether the attenuated high-feature_040 signal from H159 was confounded by feature_003, and its threshold-level result is encouraging but still conditional. I therefore request one independent validation, H165, because it is a strong complementary context and the most useful claim to test whether feature_063=1 lower outcome is replicated beyond a single discovery split. If H165 validates, the feature_063 residual signal can be described more firmly as a replicated borderline/context-specific signal; if it attenuates below threshold, feature_063 should remain a secondary, uncertain residual marker rather than a robust predictor. These conclusions remain dataset-specific associations and do not imply causality, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iter10 appraise: feature_063 now has multiple dataset contexts with entirely positive signed intervals, and three focal-negative contexts with lower bounds above the 0.15-unit threshold: H165 (feature_041=0), H166 (low feature_030), and H168 (high feature_040 excluding feature_003). H167 (low feature_040) and H169 (high feature_030 excluding feature_003) are suggestive but below threshold. These contexts overlap and are not independent replicates. Validate H165 as the strongest complementary context. If validation succeeds, treat feature_063 as a replicated residual signal but still context-sensitive; if it fails, keep it borderline. Continuous and common binary residual screens remain null or infeasible. Central dataset-specific findings remain feature_037=1 lower outcome and feature_010=1/feature_002=1 higher outcome. No causal or mechanistic claims.",
